{"id":"chatcmpl-34256f12-49f2-4073-9042-84ee3850e5ac","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245079,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-tool consensus strategy for medical image interpretation where conflicting outputs arise. The key insight is that a domain-specialist tool can override generalist vision-language models when the specialist provides a specific, localized finding. A verification step is essential to adjudicate conflicts before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Specialist-over-generalist precedence: when a domain-specific expert tool reports a specific localized finding while generalist tools report negatives, weight the specialist's output more heavily, especially for subtle findings.\",\n    \"Multi-source triangulation: query at least two independent tools with different strengths (specialist reasoning, grounded localization, general VLM QA) to cross-validate the same clinical question.\",\n    \"Conflict-triggered verification: when tool outputs disagree, invoke an explicit verification step that states the conflict and proposed answer before finalizing, rather than silently picking one.\",\n    \"Laterality disambiguation: for paired-structure questions (left vs right), explicitly ask each tool to specify side and describe supporting signs (opacity, volume loss, silhouette sign) to reduce side-confusion errors.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Use a specialist model for the primary read, a grounded/localization model to confirm location, and a general VLM for independent cross-check; resolve disagreements via explicit verification.\",\n    \"Binary choice with paired options\": \"Always force tools to state which side/structure and the supporting evidence, since paired options are prone to side-swap errors.\",\n    \"Conflicting tool outputs\": \"Do not average or default to majority; instead surface the conflict to a verifier with the proposed answer and rationale.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before answering, confirm at least one tool explicitly named the laterality (left/right) and cited a supporting imaging sign.\",\n    \"If any tool disagrees, run a verification step that records the conflict and the proposed answer prior to finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":604,"total_tokens":1018,"completion_tokens":414,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":604},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":414}}}